## 1. Result in one paragraph

kexec from a Pocketboot resident whose MDP5 pipeline is scanning out over HDMI into a second Pocketboot kernel,
same MSM8916 apps SMMU context bank cb=4 (`1e24000.iommu-ctx`, fixed ASID 4). Without any invalidate (BASE),
every hop faulted: 3/3 smaller-to-larger-mode hops with the first fault at exactly the IOVA where the source's
mapped extent ended (0x386000), plus the same-mode hop (S1) that the model had predicted to be silent, which
faulted inside the source map instead. With the patch under test (NEW, invalidate inside the per-context loop
before programming TTBR0) 3/3 hops were clean; with the shipped placement (OLD, invalidate after the loop) 3/3
were clean; a chained NEW->NEW generation-2 hop was clean. No OOPS, no hang, no TLB SYNC timeout, adb back 4 s
after every destination banner. 161 `Unhandled context fault` lines in the whole capture, all `cb=4`, all produced by
the four BASE destinations (a BASE resident's storm continues while it idles until the next relay pulse, so a few
lines sit just past the next row's start mark, e.g. 4528-4532 after P05's).

