## 3. Mechanism under test (from `L/notes/predict.md` section 0)

cb=4 keeps ASID 4 in both kernels, and the destination programs a new TTBR0 and re-enables the context without any
TLBI, so the SMMU's ASID-tagged leaf TLB and intermediate walk-cache entries from the source survive (TTBR/TCR/SCTLR
writes never invalidate; only TLBIALL/TLBIASID/TLBIVA do, and the global space belongs to TZ). Stale leaf entries
translate silently to the source's old physical pages, while stale intermediate entries send the walk into the
source's old table pages, whose entries beyond what the source ever mapped are zero, so the destination faults
(FSR.TF) exactly on IOVAs at or beyond the source's mapped extent = `0x2000 + k_S * size(S)` (a 4 KiB `tx_gem`
sits at 0x1000 and the dumb buffers pack from 0x2000; measured 0x386000 for 640x480 and 0xa8e000 for 1280x720 in
`runs/*/pre-iovas.txt`).

Discriminating arm: source in a SMALLER mode than the destination. Pocketboot maps a 4 KiB `tx_gem` at 0x1000
then three dumb buffers packed from 0x2000: 640x480 = 3 x 1228800 B -> extent end 0x386000; 1280x720 =
3 x 3686400 B at 0x2000/0x386000/0x70a000 -> extent end 0xa8e000. S=640x480 -> D=1280x720 therefore puts the
destination's second and third buffers beyond the source extent, first fault predicted at 0x386000.

