## 6. What it shows, and where it disagrees with the prediction

1. The stale-TLB hazard is real on this SMMU across kexec and reproduces deterministically: 3/3 BASE hops faulted
   on cb=4 with the first fault at 0x386000, the exact end of the source's mapped extent as the code model
   predicted (predict.md section 5 row 1, "pattern A": no fault IOVA below the extent, `faults_outside_source_map=10,
   inside=0`). The fault signature (fsr 0x40000202, fsynr 0x23 PLVL=3, cb=4) is the same encoding as the A5 line
   in the commit message. The fault set is the rate limiter's 10 samples per 5 s; the suppressed counts show
   ~14k faults/s sustained for as long as the destination scans out, with continuous INTF1 underruns.
2. 390b5df1 (NEW) removes the faults: 3/3 hops clean at the identical destination allocation, 4 CPUs, msm
   initialised, adb back, one modeset underrun each (baseline), no TLB SYNC timeout (so the reviewers' inherited-
   stalled-transaction concern, readiness W6a, did not manifest on this board). The shipped OLD placement is
   equally clean here (3/3): this board cannot distinguish the two placements because no master is fetching
   between programming and the invalidate (predict.md section 5.2); the in-loop placement's argument (a master
   already live, e.g. a bootloader-lit panel) is not exercised by this A/B.
3. The chained NEW->NEW generation-2 hop is clean with the `-22 reusing fixed region` path exercised a second time.
4. CONTRADICTION of the model: the same-mode BASE control S1 was predicted to be silent (predict.md section 0
   "S == D with equal k: NO fault expected", readiness W3) but faulted 10/10 at 0x70b000..0x70b400, all inside
   the source map (third buffer), still PLVL=3. Unlike the S<D storms these faults were transient: 10 lines within
   ~120 ms (2.214-2.331 s, UART 9049-9060), no `callbacks suppressed` line anywhere in the S1 window and nothing
   after 2.48 s, and they hit only buffer 3 (0x70a000, not the active scanout buffer after the hop) while the active
   buffer 0x386000 never faulted. A leaf-level translation fault on an IOVA the source had mapped
   means the walk went through a stale cached L2->L3 pointer into the OLD L3 table page whose memory the
   destination kernel had already recycled (predict.md section 5.1 "pattern B"). Consequence: BASE is unsafe
   even when the destination maps exactly the source's IOVAs; the "silent stale picture" case was not observed
   on this board and the hazard is not limited to S<D. Interpretation, not a measurement: the fault line does not
   say which level's cache was stale; the leaf-level PLVL on a mapped IOVA is the inference. S1 carried no EXPECT
   and its `expect_match` is null in `result.json`.
5. Other prediction misses, all harmless to the A/B: readiness W1 (Pocketboot would pick 1024x768 for the
   640x480 FIT) was moot after c90012f (C2 ran at 640x480); C5 showed the kernel does not honour
   `video=HDMI-A-1:1920x1080@30e` on this bridge (`runs/C5-cold-1920x1080/cold-dmesg.txt:282`: `msm_mdp
   1a01000.display-controller: [drm] User-defined mode not supported: "1920x1080": 30 80192 ...`, i.e. mode_valid
   rejected the 80.192 MHz CVT mode and the crtc fell back to a DRIVER 1280x720 mode), so
   the 1920x1080 destinations were unused; W4 (BASE storm stalls adb -> HUNG) did not happen.

## 7. Anomalies and caveats

- A1: Pocketboot's kmsg tracing level defaults to WARN (`pocketboot/src/kmsg.rs:19`), no cmdline carries
  `pocketboot.log=info`, so `starting frankenSlint UI ... width= height=`, `POCKETBOOT_DRM_READY` and the
  `POCKETBOOT_DRM_PAGE_FLIP_TEST_*` lines never appeared; mode and flip completion were taken from
  `dri/0/state` (crtc mode, active=1) and `dri/0/gem` (3 dumb buffers mapped) instead. Only `WARN pocketboot: no
  boot entries discovered` is Pocketboot's.
- A2: the destination's 1280x720 mode type varied between rows (P01 `0x20` USERDEF CVT 74440 kHz; P02..S3 `0x60`
  DRIVER|USERDEF CEA 74250 kHz; C5 `0x40` DRIVER only): the ADV7533 sink sense flaps and sometimes supplies a
  driver mode list. Same geometry and identical GEM allocation in every case.
- `vblank time out, crtc=0` once on P07 and once on S1 (both BASE, during the storm); never on NEW/OLD.
- No HDMI sink or capture dongle was attached: picture content (stale/garbage bands) was not observed, only
  faults and underruns. No EDID, so all modes were forced.
- Not tested here: the Samsung A5 (the commit message's original report) was not re-run with 390b5df1; HUNG/
  hang-diag/usbreset recovery paths were never exercised; the harness timing constants were never tuned (every
  timeout had slack); only one board, one SoC (MSM8916 apps SMMU, `qcom,msm-iommu-v1`), one TZ; the kernel is
  Pocketboot's 7.1-rc6+ base with out-of-tree 0001-0005 and 0007, not mainline; 0007 (fixed secure page table
  region) is required for any kexec'd qcom-iommu probe on this board and is not upstream.
- Host-side only, no board effect: `notes/rowfields.sh` (read-only jq/grep summariser) was added during the
  phase; two blank `rc=` annotations in board.md section 0 (zsh has no PIPESTATUS; the OK lines are the evidence).
- The board result JSON reports S1 `expect_match=false` because its schema needs a boolean; the file of record
  (`runs/S1-base-720-720/result.json`) has null.

